00:06:10.328 --> 00:06:11.162
And I do feel like

00:06:11.162 --> 00:06:12.413
there was a before Bridesmaids

00:06:12.413 --> 00:06:13.873
and and after bridesmaids.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.917
And and that's how I felt

00:06:15.917 --> 00:06:16.876
when I read the script

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.003
when we were making the movie.

00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:21.464
There is going to be a before

00:06:21.464 --> 00:06:22.507
and an after, and it's

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:23.007
going to be

00:06:23.007 --> 00:06:23.591
about

00:06:23.591 --> 00:06:25.301
opening people's ideas

00:06:25.301 --> 00:06:27.428
of what's possible in storytelling

00:06:27.428 --> 00:06:28.679
and what we're capable of.

00:06:28.679 --> 00:06:29.680
And the women's and girls

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.557
stories actually do sell. Yes.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:32.642
And that and that.

00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:33.851
Their stories are our stories.

00:06:33.851 --> 00:06:35.228
I grew up my whole life

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.687
